      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p8_b14",
      "text": "across many prompts, and a gradient update must fit all promptwise signals through one\nshared neural policy. Still, the decomposition is the right local picture when the model\nclass is expressive on the prompts being trained. The promptwise DRRO solution says\nwhat each prompt would like the policy to do if it could move freely; the implemented\npolicy-gradient algorithm then asks the LLM to approximate those directions as well as\nits parameterization allows. In this sense, realizability error enters as a coupling effect\nacross prompts, not as a change in the robust objective itself.\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.58,
